<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huanren</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Huanren Manchu Autonomous County</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huanren is a county in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaoning">Liaoning</a> province in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the Hun River near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a>. Korean tradition places <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jolbon">Jolbon</a>, the first capital of Goguryeo, in this area, and the nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wunu-mountain">Wunü Mountain</a> fortress is usually identified with it. The fortress is part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capital-cities-and-tombs-of-the-ancient-koguryo-kingdom">Capital Cities and Tombs of the Ancient Koguryo Kingdom</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huanren.jpg" alt="Huanren" width="320" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Wenn · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Benxi-Huanren_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
